## Bundled dependencies

The shipped application links third-party Rust crates and npm packages, each of
which keeps its own license. Their notices are listed in the dependency
manifests and lockfiles under `src-tauri/` and `web/`.

## Development tooling (not shipped)

This repository also contains development-time tooling that is **not part of any
released artifact**. The macOS and Windows bundles are built from `web/dist`
plus the Rust binary; none of the files below are compiled into or distributed
with them.

### Trellis — AGPL-3.0

[Trellis](https://github.com/mindfold-ai/Trellis) (Copyright mindfold.ai) is an
engineering framework for AI coding agents, licensed under the **GNU Affero
General Public License v3.0**. It is used here as a development tool.

Files in this repository that originate from Trellis templates:

| Path | Notes |
| --- | --- |
| `.trellis/scripts/` | Python helper scripts invoked by the hooks below |
| `.trellis/workflow.md` | Phase definitions, regenerated by `trellis update` |
| `.trellis/agents/` | Sub-agent role definitions |
| `.trellis/.template-hashes.json` | Update tracking |
| `.claude/hooks/` | Session hooks (SessionStart / UserPromptSubmit / PreToolUse) |
| `.claude/agents/trellis-*.md` | Sub-agent definitions for Claude Code |
| `.claude/commands/trellis/` | Slash commands |
| `.claude/skills/trellis-*/` | Trellis-provided skills |

The `<!-- TRELLIS:START -->` … `<!-- TRELLIS:END -->` block at the end of
`AGENTS.md` is likewise Trellis-managed.

**Everything else under `.trellis/` is this project's own content and remains
MIT-licensed** — specifically `.trellis/spec/` (the coding conventions we
wrote), `.trellis/tasks/` (task artifacts) and `.trellis/workspace/`
(developer journals). `.trellis/.developer` is gitignored and never committed.

Because Trellis is AGPL-3.0 and this project is MIT, the two are kept strictly
separated: Trellis code stays in the paths listed above, is used only at
development time, and is not linked into, combined with, or distributed as part
of the released application.

If you redistribute this *repository* (as opposed to a released build), the
Trellis files above continue to be governed by AGPL-3.0; the remainder is MIT.
To drop the AGPL components entirely, run `trellis uninstall` and delete the
paths in the table above — nothing in `web/`, `src-tauri/` or `scripts/`
depends on them.
